From abb45ea98d7cb5acd9d0b6e3b291e14561a4f0e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohnnyC96 <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 05:22:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: remove the in-engine diagnostics (now the ob_diag
 plugin)

The engine keeps only the hook points of runtime/ps2_diag_hooks.h. Removed,
with their environment variables: the scripted input player
(PS2X_INPUT_SCRIPT, ps2_input_script), the frame dump (PS2X_FRAME_DUMP_DIR,
ps2_frame_dump), the frame-time log (PS2X_FRAME_TIME, EeScheduler), the guest
PC sampler (PS2X_PC_SAMPLE, ps2_pc_sampler) and the VU1 capture
(PS2X_VU1_CAPTURE, ps2_vu1_capture with its PATH1 tap). The plugin implements
them over the hooks; without a plugin the variables do nothing.

- EeScheduler: no frame-time file or sampler; sums its idle (pacing) wait only
  when a plugin is loaded, for onVsync.
- PS2Runtime: frames reach the plugin's onFrame only (external GS: copied only
  when a plugin is loaded); the external GS frame demand is the plugin's
  wantsFrame; the host loop asks onHostFrame/onShutdown; the window is hidden
  only by PS2X_HIDDEN=1 (a script no longer implies it).
- Pad: a plugin that owns the pad replaces the host pad; nothing else.
- Tests: the input script, frame dump, frame-time, PC sampler and VU1 capture
  tests move to the plugin's own test program; new tests check that, without a
  plugin, PS2X_FRAME_TIME/PS2X_PC_SAMPLE write no file and PS2X_VU1_CAPTURE
  creates no directory.
---
